      "hints": [
        "The list is already sorted, so no sort is needed. Think of the output in three parts: before, overlapping, after.",
        "First copy every interval whose end is less than the new start. Then, while an interval's start is at most the new end, absorb it into the new interval with min and max.",
        "Append the widened new interval once, then copy everything that is left."
      ],
      "solution": {
        "javascript": "function insert(intervals, newInterval) {\n  const result = []\n  let [start, end] = newInterval\n  let i = 0\n  const n = intervals.length\n  while (i < n && intervals[i][1] < start) result.push(intervals[i++])\n  while (i < n && intervals[i][0] <= end) {\n    start = Math.min(start, intervals[i][0])\n    end = Math.max(end, intervals[i][1])\n    i++\n  }\n  result.push([start, end])\n  while (i < n) result.push(intervals[i++])\n  return result\n}\n",
        "python": "def insert(intervals, new_interval):\n    result, i, n = [], 0, len(intervals)\n    start, end = new_interval\n    while i < n and intervals[i][1] < start:     # ends before the new one\n        result.append(intervals[i])\n        i += 1\n    while i < n and intervals[i][0] <= end:      # overlaps: absorb it\n        start = min(start, intervals[i][0])\n        end = max(end, intervals[i][1])\n        i += 1\n    result.append([start, end])\n    result.extend(intervals[i:])                 # everything after\n    return result\n"
      },
